*** To compile and install: ***

1) qmake  (or qmake-qt4)
2) make
3) ./regmas

Notes:
- a project file for Kdevelop is attahced. Hovewer you can use whatsoever IDE to work with the project. The interface file was generated using QTDesigner;
- you need the Qt4 development library to compile this program as well as the GLPK library.
- on some Linux distros you have to use qmake-qt4 in order to use Qt4 instead of the "old" Qt3 libraries. For the same reason on some distros when using Kdevelop you have to manually lunch the command qmake-qt4 from the console before start working on kdevelop.
- detailed compiling instructions for both Linux and Windows are available on the regmas.org web site

*** To use: ***
Please refer to the User Manual (http://www.regmas.org/doc/userManual).


